        "function": [
          "Acyltransferase involved in the biosynthesis of membrane phospholipids (PubMed:32403425). It introduces a cis-vaccenoyl group (18:1) into the sn-2 position of phospholipids (PubMed:32403425). Overproduction of YihG facilitates the synthesis of phospholipids containing a myristoyl group (14:0) and a cis-vaccenoyl group at the sn-2 position, and a cis-vaccenoyl group at the sn-1 position (PubMed:32403425). May affect flagellar formation through modulation of the fatty acyl composition of membrane phospholipids (PubMed:32403425)."
